---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

// Second rewrite of this page, for the same reason as the first: the project it
// described stopped existing.
//
// Round one was a Unity 2022.3 URP voxel world, stalled in May 2026 and
// scrapped in September. Round two was a solo sci-fi extraction shooter --
// "one map, one weapon, and a way out", 17 weeks, five outcomes about bots and
// salvage. That one was boxed on 24 September 2026 after three weeks, and
// unlike the Unity project it was boxed while it was working: the greybox
// sector finished four days early with three routes walked and timed.
//
// The temptation is to swap the nouns quietly and imply the shooter never
// happened. That is the exact failure this page exists to avoid -- backlog
// item 06 was about a page making claims it could not support. So the pivot is
// stated here, with the numbers that show the week worked. A portfolio that
// admits a project stopped is worth more than one implying an unbroken line,
// because the second kind is never true and readers know it.
//
// The clip log is gone. It belonged to the shooter's build-in-public plan, it
// never recorded a single clip, and this project captures once at the end: six
// stills and a 45-second flythrough are the deliverable itself, not a cadence.
// In its place is a shot counter reading 0 of 6, which stays there until week
// 12. An honest zero beats a placeholder reel.
//
// Both markers below stay author-set rather than derived from `new Date()`,
// for the same two reasons as before: the zero-tolerance visual suite would
// fail on every build once a week rolled over, and content that changes
// without a commit cannot be reviewed before it ships.
const PHASE_LABEL = 'Week 1 starts 28 September';
const PHASE_NOTE = '13 weeks · to 31 Dec 2026';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Walkthrough world — Build log | Timothy Creekmore"
  description="A stylised walkthrough world in Unreal Engine 5 — a forest clearing, a creek and a few buildings, shipped 31 December 2026 as six stills and a flythrough. Timothy Creekmore."
  ogDescription="A stylised walkthrough world in Unreal Engine 5 — six stills, one flythrough, one hard deadline."
>
  <div class="grid-field" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <Nav active="game" />

  <main id="main-content" class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6">

    <header class="pt-16 pb-14">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-4">Build log &middot; Unreal Engine 5</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl mb-5">
        A small place worth standing in — by 31 December.
      </h1>
      <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed max-w-xl mb-4">
        A stylised walkthrough world: a forest clearing, a creek with a small bridge, and a handful of buildings. No combat and no systems — it is built to be worth looking at and pleasant to walk through, and it is judged on six images and a short video.
      </p>
      <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed max-w-xl mb-6">
        It replaces an extraction shooter that was stopped deliberately, three weeks in, while it was working. That story is at the bottom of this page rather than hidden from it.
      </p>
      <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-gray-200 px-4 py-2 text-sm text-gray-600">
        <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full" style="background: var(--accent);" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        {PHASE_LABEL}
      </span>
    </header>

    <!-- Five checkable outcomes, as before. The difference is that these are
         artefacts rather than behaviours: a reader can see whether six images
         exist without installing anything. -->
    <section aria-labelledby="done-heading" class="rule pt-8 pb-10">
      <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between mb-6">
        <h2 id="done-heading" class="eyebrow">What done means</h2>
        <p class="tick">31 Dec 2026</p>
      </div>
      <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed max-w-xl mb-6">
        Not &ldquo;the world is finished&rdquo; — a place is never finished, and that is how projects like this die. Done is five things that either exist or do not:
      </p>
      <ol class="list-none p-0 m-0 max-w-xl">
        <li class="grid grid-cols-[1.75rem_1fr] gap-2 pb-3">
          <span class="tick pt-1">01</span>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Six hero shots, from fixed camera positions chosen in week 2.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="grid grid-cols-[1.75rem_1fr] gap-2 pb-3">
          <span class="tick pt-1">02</span>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">A 45-second flythrough.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="grid grid-cols-[1.75rem_1fr] gap-2 pb-3">
          <span class="tick pt-1">03</span>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">A packaged build you can walk around in — interactive, not a render.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="grid grid-cols-[1.75rem_1fr] gap-2 pb-3">
          <span class="tick pt-1">04</span>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">A photo mode: free camera, depth of field, a couple of filters.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="grid grid-cols-[1.75rem_1fr] gap-2">
          <span class="tick pt-1">05</span>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">All of it published here, where you are reading this.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed max-w-xl mt-6">
        One scene, roughly 100 by 100 metres. No open world, no second location.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="rules-heading" class="rule pt-8 pb-10">
      <h2 id="rules-heading" class="eyebrow mb-8">The rules that make it shippable</h2>
      <div class="max-w-xl">
        <div class="rule-b pb-4 mb-4">
          <p class="font-semibold text-gray-900 text-sm mb-1">Order of operations decides everything</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Anything that moves other things comes first: terrain moves trees, water carves terrain, the village footprint moves both. Grass moves nothing, so it is last. Plant before blocking out and half of it gets deleted.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rule-b pb-4 mb-4">
          <p class="font-semibold text-gray-900 text-sm mb-1">One asset pack, one artist</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Stylised work falls apart when packs are mixed — outline weight, colour and shape language never agree between artists. Coherence beats variety, and it is what makes this affordable solo.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rule-b pb-4 mb-4">
          <p class="font-semibold text-gray-900 text-sm mb-1">The style comes from light, not shaders</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Time of day, fog and a colour grade do the work. A hand-written cel shader in week four is the rabbit hole that eats the deadline.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rule-b pb-4 mb-4">
          <p class="font-semibold text-gray-900 text-sm mb-1">Detail only where the camera looks</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">The six shots are chosen before any dressing starts. Work outside them is invisible by definition.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rule-b pb-4">
          <p class="font-semibold text-gray-900 text-sm mb-1">Ship it rough over ship it late</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Kept from the last plan, because it is the rule that survived contact. A modest scene published on 31 December beats a better one still being lit in March.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="roadmap-heading" class="rule pt-8 pb-10">
      <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between mb-8">
        <h2 id="roadmap-heading" class="eyebrow">Roadmap</h2>
        <p class="tick">{PHASE_NOTE}</p>
      </div>

      <ol class="list-none p-0 m-0">
        <li class="grid grid-cols-[1.5rem_1fr] gap-4 pb-6">
          <span class="phase-dot wip" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div>
            <p class="tick float-right">Weeks 1–3 &middot; Sep–Oct</p>
            <p class="font-semibold text-gray-900 text-sm mb-1">Phase 1 · Block it out</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Terrain sculpted grey — the clearing, the creek bed, the shelf the village sits on. Buildings and bridge as plain boxes. A rough lighting pass so the shapes can be judged, then the six camera positions get chosen and written down.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="grid grid-cols-[1.5rem_1fr] gap-4 pb-6">
          <span class="phase-dot todo" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div>
            <p class="tick float-right">Weeks 4–5 &middot; Oct</p>
            <p class="font-semibold text-gray-500 text-sm mb-1">Phase 2 · Ground and water</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">The creek, which carves the terrain as it goes and so has to arrive before anything is planted. Then the landscape material — grass, dirt, rock, and mud at the water's edge.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="grid grid-cols-[1.5rem_1fr] gap-4 pb-6">
          <span class="phase-dot todo" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div>
            <p class="tick float-right">Weeks 6–10 &middot; Nov–Dec</p>
            <p class="font-semibold text-gray-500 text-sm mb-1">Phase 3 · Dress it</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">Foliage biggest to smallest — trees for silhouette, then bushes, then grass to hide the seams. The blockout boxes become real buildings, props go where the shots look, and a detail pass softens every hard line where things meet the ground.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="grid grid-cols-[1.5rem_1fr] gap-4">
          <span class="phase-dot todo" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div>
            <p class="tick float-right">Weeks 11–13 &middot; Dec</p>
            <p class="font-semibold text-gray-500 text-sm mb-1">Phase 4 · Finish it</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">The real lighting pass, which is where a stylised scene is won or lost. Then photo mode, the six captures, the flythrough, a packaged build, and publishing — with four days of buffer that are deliberately empty.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <!-- The pivot, stated plainly and with numbers. This section is why the
         rest of the page can be believed: anyone can see what the previous
         project was, when it stopped, and what existed at the time. -->
    <section aria-labelledby="pivot-heading" class="rule pt-8 pb-10">
      <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between mb-6">
        <h2 id="pivot-heading" class="eyebrow">What happened to the shooter</h2>
        <p class="tick">Boxed 24 Sep 2026</p>
      </div>
      <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed max-w-xl mb-4">
        For three weeks this page described a solo sci-fi extraction shooter, and it got further than the Unity project ever did. By the end of week three there was a 200-metre greybox sector with three routes from spawn to extraction, each walked and timed: <span class="tick">55.6s</span> across the open middle, <span class="tick">77.1s</span> through a covered warren, <span class="tick">75.4s</span> the long way round. A working extraction loop — walk in, hold five seconds, get out. That week's goal was met four days early.
      </p>
      <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed max-w-xl mb-4">
        It was stopped anyway. The weeks ahead were enemy AI, weapon feel, loot tables and balancing — months of systems work, for a first shipped game, by someone whose interest is art, light and level design. Continuing meant choosing the least interesting version of the next fourteen weeks.
      </p>
      <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed max-w-xl">
        Nothing was thrown away. The sector, the loop and the notes are tagged in the repository at the point they stopped, and the workflow around them — the plan, the board, the session log — carried straight over to this project. Stopping something that works is a different act from abandoning something that does not, and only one of the two is worth repeating.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Deliberately empty until week 12, with the same discipline as the clip
         log it replaces: a placeholder image would repeat the failure this page
         was first rewritten to fix. -->
    <section aria-labelledby="shots-heading" class="rule pt-8 pb-16">
      <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between mb-6">
        <h2 id="shots-heading" class="eyebrow">The shots</h2>
        <p class="tick">0 of 6</p>
      </div>
      <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed max-w-xl">
        Six images and one flythrough, captured in week 12 from positions chosen in week 2. Nothing appears here before then — the scene spends nine weeks as grey shapes, bare terrain and half-planted trees, and none of that is worth showing.
      </p>
    </section>

  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
